From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:11:09 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpu: apple,agx: allow explicit non-coherent DMA

The J713 GPU now declares dma-noncoherent to retain its qualified DMA
path on CPUs with LoC zero. Permit that standard property in the GPU
binding so the device tree validates against the same contract.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>

(cherry picked from commit ec3215d8470e06c4d61194e59f1aee4983634bab)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,agx.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,agx.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,agx.yaml
index 0118e3afa2..daef8fd85a 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,agx.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/apple,agx.yaml
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@ properties:
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  dma-noncoherent: true
+
   mboxes:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 2
